repository-code: 'https://github.com/Gemmate-Technologies/nanocarbon'
abstract: >-
  nanocarbon is a Python library which builds atomistic models of
  amorphous nanoporous carbon from a specified pore size distribution,
  pore volume fraction and carbon density. The pore size distribution may
  be an analytical form or a tabulated curve, digitized from a measurement
  or computed on another structure. Pores drawn from it are placed first,
  carbon is then grown around them ring by ring up to the target density,
  and each structure is written as LAMMPS input for a molecular dynamics
  anneal, with the pores held as walls. The same routines characterize any
  structure, constructed or imported from a trajectory, through its pore
  size distribution, porosity, accessible surface and volume, radial
  distribution function, ring statistics, coordination and pore
  connectivity. When the construction parameters are not known, a particle
  swarm optimizer recovers them from target quantities, measured on a
  laboratory sample or computed on a reference structure, such as the
  density, the pore size distribution, the porosity, the accessible
  surface area, the pore volume and the radial distribution function.
keywords:
